Suggests: software-properties-common
Description: unified package manager for APT, Flatpak and AppImage
 Shelly-APT is a Debian port of Shelly, the Arch Linux package manager.
 It manages APT packages, local .deb files, Flatpaks and AppImages from one
 command-line tool (`shelly`) and one GTK4/libadwaita application
 (`shelly-ui`), with shortcodes such as `shelly -Is htop`, transaction
 previews, downgrades, holds, repository and signing-key management,
 conffile review, backups and background update notifications.
